# Interview Answer (2-minute version)

> Attention allows a model to focus on the most relevant parts of the input while processing a sequence. Instead of compressing an entire sentence into a single vector as in Seq2Seq, attention dynamically assigns weights to different words. Transformers build on this idea using self-attention, where every token can attend to every other token. They use Query, Key, and Value vectors to compute attention scores, enabling parallel processing, better long-range dependency modeling, and superior scalability compared to RNNs and LSTMs.

A strong interview explanation is to first explain **the problem with Seq2Seq**, then **how Attention solves it**, and finally **how Transformers generalize Attention and remove recurrence entirely**. That's the conceptual journey interviewers usually want to hear.
